id: pm-graph-bfal
title: Enhance pm-graph impact to use canonical registry-aware pm graph engine with graceful fallback and diagram rendering
description: "Delegate pm pm-graph impact to the canonical pm graph impact engine (registry-aware, honors custom relationship kinds) with graceful fallback to the existing reverseReachable path on older pm-cli. Add --direction/--depth/--limit/--format flags, build an impact subgraph projector for --format mermaid|dot|graphml diagrams, and keep the back-compat result shape."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-23T17:54:47.224Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-23T19:12:47.203Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-23T18:11:09.507Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: "pm pm-graph impact now delegates to the canonical registry-aware pm graph engine (rich affected rows + cost), preserves the back-compat shape, supports --direction/--depth/--limit/--format, renders mermaid/dot/graphml diagrams, and falls back to reverseReachable on older pm-cli. devDependency bumped to ^2026.7.23; peer floor unchanged."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-23T19:12:47.203Z",claude-orchestrator,"Review round 1 (CodeRabbit, 3 valid findings) addressed: (1) canonical path now post-filters affected rows by the shaped item-id set so --filter/--include-closed apply on both engines; (2) count derived from impacted.length (back-compat invariant); (3) canonical-only tests gated on pmGraphImpactAvailable. --include-closed routed to shaped-graph fallback (canonical engine is active-only, no closed switch); upstream/both + --include-closed fails loud with an accurate message. Added 2 regression tests (--filter type parity + include-closed routing/error). 94/94 tests pass."
close_reason: "Implemented canonical pm graph impact engine delegation with graceful fallback, direction mapping, impact subgraph projectors, and diagram rendering"
body: ""
